    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d193">

                <pb facs="0342" n="240" xml:id="pg240"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.0011 Mutual Guarantee (Eastern Locarno)/122:
                    Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in the Soviet Union</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Wiley</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                        State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Moscow</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1935-04-09T16:00:00+03:00">April 9, 1935—4
                            p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received April 9—2:45 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>138. According to information received from Lithuanian Minister, Litvinov
                    yesterday formally asked Estonian and Latvian Ministers to inform him within 2
                    days whether their Governments would be willing to enter into a pact of
                    automatic mutual assistance together with the Soviet Union, France,
                    Czechoslovakia and Lithuania. Lithuania he said had no other alternative but to
                    enter such a pact. He did not indicate, however, whether Lithuania would do so
                    independently of the other two Baltic States. He expressed concern over Polish
                    influence on Estonian foreign policy.</p>
                <p>Repeated Riga.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Wiley</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
